    desc: "Complete 28-page walkthrough of the homebuying process",
    content: `# First-Time Homebuyer Guide\n\n## Introduction\nBuying your first home is one of the most important financial decisions of your life. This guide walks you through every step of the process, from checking your credit to getting your keys.\n\n## Chapter 1: Are You Ready?\nAssess your financial health before beginning. Review your credit score, calculate your debt-to-income ratio, and ensure you have adequate savings for down payment and closing costs.\n\n## Chapter 2: Getting Pre-Approved\nWork with a licensed mortgage loan originator to get pre-approved before shopping for homes. Pre-approval strengthens your offer and helps you shop in the right price range.\n\n## Chapter 3: Finding Your Home\nDefine your priorities, work with a buyer's agent, and evaluate neighborhoods based on schools, commute, safety, and long-term value.\n\n## Chapter 4: Making an Offer\nYour agent will help you craft a competitive offer. Understand contingencies, earnest money, and negotiation strategies.\n\n## Chapter 5: Under Contract\nAfter offer acceptance, you'll complete inspections, appraisal, and final loan approval. Stay in close contact with your lender during this period.\n\n## Chapter 6: Closing\nReview your Closing Disclosure, bring required funds, sign documents, and receive your keys.\n\n---\nPrepared by ${ADVISOR.name} | NMLS #${ADVISOR.nmls} | ${ADVISOR.email}\nApply at: ${APP_LINK}`
